WEBVTT

00:00:01.795 --> 00:00:04.635
Well, of course I haven't seen him.
If I was looking I'd find him.

00:00:04.795 --> 00:00:06.715
Hank! There you are.

00:00:06.875 --> 00:00:08.355
-Hurry up!
-Okay. Okay.

00:00:08.515 --> 00:00:13.755
K. It starts with a "k."
Kid z-own-y. Kid zone!

00:00:13.955 --> 00:00:15.875
No! No kids. Kids grab things.

00:00:15.955 --> 00:00:17.835
And I'm not losing
another tentacle for you.

00:00:17.995 --> 00:00:20.555
You lost a tentacle?
Well then you're not an octopus,

00:00:20.635 --> 00:00:21.875
you're a septopus.

00:00:22.035 --> 00:00:23.355
I may not remember, but I can count.

00:00:23.515 --> 00:00:24.835
-Hurry up!
-Okay.

00:00:24.955 --> 00:00:28.395
Journey to the-- Hey, look. Shells.

00:00:28.675 --> 00:00:29.515
(GASPS)

00:00:30.995 --> 00:00:32.435
Hey, look. Shells!

00:00:32.515 --> 00:00:33.795
(CHARLIE CHUCKLING)

00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:35.515
Daddy, here's a shell for you.

00:00:35.675 --> 00:00:38.155
That's great, Dory.
You found another one.

00:00:38.355 --> 00:00:40.395
-I did?
-Oh, yes, you did.

00:00:40.555 --> 00:00:41.955
You're getting good at this, Dory.

00:00:42.835 --> 00:00:43.835
(FISH LAUGHING)

00:00:45.155 --> 00:00:46.515
Hey, look. Shells!

00:00:46.595 --> 00:00:47.915
(JENNY CHUCKLES)

00:00:48.035 --> 00:00:51.115
-Hey, I live there.
-Yes! Yes, indeed.

00:00:51.235 --> 00:00:54.515
-I like shells.
-(LAUGHS) That's right, dear.

00:00:56.195 --> 00:00:58.355
Do you think you could find me
another shell?

00:00:59.075 --> 00:01:00.715
(WHISPERS) Purple ones
are my favorite.

00:01:02.835 --> 00:01:04.195
Okay, Mommy.

00:01:05.875 --> 00:01:08.675
Mommy. Purple shell. Purple shell!
Hey, my home had a purple shell.

00:01:11.075 --> 00:01:13.195
So what? Half the exhibits here
have purple shells in them.

00:01:13.395 --> 00:01:15.195
No, no, no. You don't understand.
I remember her now.

00:01:15.395 --> 00:01:17.955
Purple shells were her favorite
and she had this adorable giggle.

00:01:18.075 --> 00:01:19.355
And then my dad was really friendly.

00:01:19.515 --> 00:01:20.875
And now your wacky memory's
gonna get us caught.

00:01:25.235 --> 00:01:26.515
Still think this is destiny?

00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:28.195
-Hank, we have to find my folks!
-Quiet!

00:01:34.915 --> 00:01:38.275
Ugh. Base, this is Carol.

00:01:38.435 --> 00:01:41.555
Uh, I think I might have found
that missing octopus. Over.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:43.955
-See what you did?
-Sorry.

00:01:44.115 --> 00:01:45.435
This could not be worse.

00:01:45.635 --> 00:01:49.795
Hmm. "Destiny." (GASPS) Destiny.

00:01:49.955 --> 00:01:52.595
-Hank. I got a feeling.
-Sh!

00:01:52.715 --> 00:01:53.755
I think we should get in the bucket.

00:01:53.915 --> 00:01:56.075
-No. Stop.
-Seriously. It says "destiny" and it is--

00:01:56.235 --> 00:01:57.795
-No, no, no, no, no.
-We've got to get in that bucket.

00:01:57.915 --> 00:02:02.235
-I'm not going with you in that bucket.
-Here...I...go...in...the...bucket. Bye.

00:02:03.555 --> 00:02:04.555
(GASPS)

00:02:04.635 --> 00:02:09.435
Hey, guys, I'm looking for my family.
Oh, good idea. Play dead.

00:02:11.315 --> 00:02:12.795
(HANK GASPS)

00:02:16.155 --> 00:02:19.515
I'm sorry. I got to blink. How do you
hold your eyes open that long?

00:02:20.475 --> 00:02:21.475
(GRUNTING)

00:02:27.675 --> 00:02:28.675
(GROANS)

00:02:30.795 --> 00:02:33.835
Hey, guys. Wait a second.

00:02:34.115 --> 00:02:35.115
(SCREAMS)

00:02:37.035 --> 00:02:38.035
(PANTING)

00:02:39.595 --> 00:02:40.635
(SCREAMS)

00:02:40.875 --> 00:02:43.635
Our next guest
has been here a very long time.

00:02:43.795 --> 00:02:47.795
She's a whale shark.
Her name is Destiny.

00:02:47.915 --> 00:02:49.195
Destiny? Really?

00:02:49.315 --> 00:02:52.355
You'll notice she's extremely
nearsighted and has trouble...

00:02:52.515 --> 00:02:56.795
navigating her environment.
Oh! And here she comes now.

00:02:56.915 --> 00:03:00.395
Ooh! Destiny. (GASPS) You're a fish?

00:03:00.475 --> 00:03:01.475
(DESTINY GROANS)

00:03:02.275 --> 00:03:03.755
Wait. What?

00:03:03.875 --> 00:03:06.875
-Hi! Hello there.
-Whoa! Oh. Whoa.

00:03:08.315 --> 00:03:09.995
All right, I'll go with you.

00:03:10.875 --> 00:03:14.315
-Excuse me.
-Is that blue blob talking?

00:03:14.475 --> 00:03:16.835
-Can you help me? I lost my family.
-You lost your family?

00:03:16.995 --> 00:03:18.235
Well, it's a long story,

00:03:18.315 --> 00:03:20.035
and truth be told,
I don't remember most of it.

00:03:20.155 --> 00:03:21.755
Aw, that is so sad.
You poor thi-- (SCREAMS)

00:03:23.595 --> 00:03:24.595
(DESTINY PANTING)

00:03:25.195 --> 00:03:28.515
Sorry. Not a great swimmer.
I can't see very well.

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.115
Oh, I think you swim beautifully.

00:03:30.195 --> 00:03:32.195
In fact, I've never seen a fish
swim like that before.

00:03:32.355 --> 00:03:34.075
(VOCALIZING) Thank you.

00:03:34.195 --> 00:03:36.675
(VOCALIZING) You're welcome.

00:03:36.875 --> 00:03:37.995
Wait. Say that again.

00:03:38.115 --> 00:03:41.035
Um, you're (VOCALIZING) welcome.

00:03:41.195 --> 00:03:42.715
-Dory?
-Yes.

00:03:42.875 --> 00:03:43.875
-Dory?
-Yes.

00:03:43.995 --> 00:03:44.955
-Dory?
-Yes.

00:03:45.075 --> 00:03:46.635
-(GASPS) Dory!
-Yes.

00:03:46.795 --> 00:03:48.955
-You and I were friends!
-No!

00:03:49.075 --> 00:03:51.035
-Dory, it's me! Destiny!
-You know me?

00:03:51.195 --> 00:03:53.875
Of course! We talked through the pipes
when we were little.

00:03:54.035 --> 00:03:55.675
-We were pipe pals!
-We were?

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:59.075
-(GASPS) Aw, you're so pretty.
-So you know where I'm from?

00:03:59.235 --> 00:04:01.115
Yep, you are from
the Open Ocean exhibit.

00:04:01.635 --> 00:04:03.035
I'm from the Open Ocean exhibit?

00:04:03.195 --> 00:04:04.795
(GASPS) Then that's
where my parents are.

00:04:04.875 --> 00:04:06.155
We got to go. Can you take me there?

00:04:06.315 --> 00:04:08.955
Uh... Kind of tough for a whale
to travel around here.

00:04:09.155 --> 00:04:12.435
Can you please keep it down
over there? My head hurts.

00:04:12.515 --> 00:04:13.515
-(DESTINY GROANS)
-Who's that?

00:04:13.595 --> 00:04:14.635
(WHISPERING)
That's my neighbor, Bailey.

00:04:14.715 --> 00:04:16.075
He was brought in with a head injury.

00:04:16.235 --> 00:04:17.315
I know you're talking about me, Destiny.

00:04:17.475 --> 00:04:19.595
He thinks he can't use his echolocation,
but I've overheard...

00:04:19.755 --> 00:04:21.835
the doctors talking.
There's not a thing wrong with him.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.915
Hear every word
you're saying about me.

00:04:24.035 --> 00:04:25.075
What's echolocation?

00:04:25.235 --> 00:04:28.155
Bailey's head is supposed to put out
a call and the echo helps him...

00:04:28.315 --> 00:04:33.355
find objects far away.
Oh, but apparently he's still "healing."

00:04:33.515 --> 00:04:35.315
Now I know you're talking about me.

00:04:35.435 --> 00:04:37.235
-I really can't echolocate.
-Oh.

00:04:37.435 --> 00:04:39.115
I cannot have this conversation again.
I just can't.

00:04:39.275 --> 00:04:42.315
I hit my head very hard out there.
See how swollen it is!

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.795
Your head is supposed to be big!
You're a beluga!

00:04:44.955 --> 00:04:46.715
Echolocation.

00:04:46.795 --> 00:04:49.355
Oh, like the world's
most powerful pair of glasses?

00:04:49.435 --> 00:04:50.595
-What?
-What are glasses?

00:04:50.715 --> 00:04:52.515
It's sort of like you go, "hoo"

00:04:52.595 --> 00:04:55.395
and then you see things.
Why do I know that?

00:04:55.515 --> 00:04:57.915
Oh. That's interesting.

00:05:00.595 --> 00:05:03.315
There you are!
Listen up, you and I are square.

00:05:03.475 --> 00:05:05.995
I took you to the map,
now give me that tag!

00:05:06.155 --> 00:05:08.195
Wait, no. I know where my parents are.
They're in the--

00:05:08.355 --> 00:05:11.195
What's it called? The place--
The soap and lotion?

00:05:11.355 --> 00:05:13.035
-BOTH: Open Ocean.
-Open Ocean!

00:05:13.195 --> 00:05:15.675
(GASPS) Open Ocean!
I know where that is.

00:05:15.835 --> 00:05:18.955
That's the exhibit located right next to--
I don't care.

00:05:19.115 --> 00:05:19.955
-Easy!
-(DESTINY GASPS)

00:05:20.035 --> 00:05:22.955
If you're trying to get to the Open Ocean
exhibit go through the pipes.

00:05:23.115 --> 00:05:25.355
-HANK: Through the pipes. Great.
-Through the pipes?

00:05:25.515 --> 00:05:27.515
Yep. Take two lefts, swim straight
and you'll hit it.

00:05:27.675 --> 00:05:31.755
Oh, that's a lot of directions. That's--
Did you get that, Hank? All that?

00:05:31.875 --> 00:05:33.795
-Uh, yeah.
-Great! Let's go.

00:05:34.315 --> 00:05:37.395
I'm not going with you. I won't fit.
You have to go by yourself.

00:05:38.075 --> 00:05:39.075
Um...

00:05:41.155 --> 00:05:46.195
That's-- I'm-- I-- See, I can't because
I'm not so good with directions.

00:05:46.355 --> 00:05:49.395
Well, that's too bad. A deal's a deal.
You wanted to find your parents?

00:05:49.555 --> 00:05:51.515
That's how you get to them.
Now give me your tag.

00:05:51.715 --> 00:05:54.555
But, Hank, I can't go in the pipes alone.
I'll forget where I'm going.

00:05:54.675 --> 00:05:57.595
-Not my problem. Tag!
-But I can't get in that way.

00:05:57.715 --> 00:06:00.715
-I'm sorry, but there's no other way.
-There's no other way. (GASPS)

00:06:01.595 --> 00:06:02.595
(GRUNTS)

00:06:02.675 --> 00:06:05.995
-There's no other way.
-Now, now. Don't panic.

00:06:06.155 --> 00:06:10.235
It's okay. Not everything in life is
easy to do. Isn't that right, Charlie?

00:06:10.395 --> 00:06:14.515
She's right. When something's
too hard, you should just give up.

00:06:14.675 --> 00:06:16.595
-Charlie!
-A joke. I'm kidding!

00:06:16.755 --> 00:06:20.395
Just a joke. A joke.
Caution, joker at work.

00:06:20.555 --> 00:06:21.835
-Joke. I got it.
-(BABY DORY LAUGHS)

00:06:22.035 --> 00:06:25.195
You see, kelpcake?
There's always another way.

